{"uid":"bc5bbc70f601d63","name":"test_q_fixture_and_silent_prelude_depths_disclosed_residual_after_the_cure","fullName":"tests.test_hub_real_render_cap_whole_call#test_q_fixture_and_silent_prelude_depths_disclosed_residual_after_the_cure","historyId":"7ba88b88c7baa3410aca85fd0476ceef","time":{"start":1791956512830,"stop":1791956516709,"duration":3879},"description":"Task 013's own cure for the disclosed residual this node used to\n    pin: PRD Q's own canonical fixture and both silent-prelude depths,\n    through the REAL whole call on both surfaces, once the LATEST\n    iteration also carries a `render_index.json` (task 012) -- the side\n    index whose whole point was to let a bounded reader resume rendering\n    from a checkpoint instead of paying for the SILENT flood between the\n    deciding `thinking_start` transition and the transcript's own end.\n\n    `ui_server.rendered_log_lines` (`render_index.bounded_tail`, both its\n    live `/logs` branch and its dead-run on-disk fallback -- neither of\n    `_fetch_live_tail`/`_fetch_dead_tail`'s own outer doubling loop even\n    runs once this index is present) now answers every one of these three\n    fixtures for comfortably UNDER the frozen 1,000,000-byte cap this same\n    node used to measure at 1,445,567 / 12,115,567 / 12,862,467 bytes --\n    and the render is still exactly correct: the full, unbounded render's\n    own last two lines, no replay, no added blank line, regardless of how\n    many silent bytes (1,000 vs. 10,000 padded gap lines, prelude depth\n    1,000 vs. 1,700) sit between the deciding line and the transcript's\n    own end.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 013's own cure for the disclosed residual this node used to<br />\npin: PRD Q's own canonical fixture and both silent-prelude depths,<br />\nthrough the REAL whole call on both surfaces, once the LATEST<br />\niteration also carries a <code>render_index.json</code> (task 012) -- the side<br />\nindex whose whole point was to let a bounded reader resume rendering<br />\nfrom a checkpoint instead of paying for the SILENT flood between the<br />\ndeciding <code>thinking_start</code> transition and the transcript's own end.</p>\n<pre><code>`ui_server.rendered_log_lines` (`render_index.bounded_tail`, both its\nlive `/logs` branch and its dead-run on-disk fallback -- neither of\n`_fetch_live_tail`/`_fetch_dead_tail`'s own outer doubling loop even\nruns once this index is present) now answers every one of these three\nfixtures for comfortably UNDER the frozen 1,000,000-byte cap this same\nnode used to measure at 1,445,567 / 12,115,567 / 12,862,467 bytes --\nand the render is still exactly correct: the full, unbounded render's\nown last two lines, no replay, no added blank line, regardless of how\nmany silent bytes (1,000 vs. 10,000 padded gap lines, prelude depth\n1,000 vs. 1,700) sit between the deciding line and the transcript's\nown end.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791956453376,"stop":1791956453377,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791956453377,"stop":1791956453377,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791956512822,"stop":1791956512822,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791956512822,"stop":1791956512824,"duration":2},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachme